1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,314
Generative media moves fast, but approved assets often lose their history.

2
00:00:05,314 --> 00:00:17,390
Teams need to know which prompt created a file, which version it came from, where the canonical copy lives, and whether those bytes have changed.

3
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:21,738
Provenance Studio turns every generation into a verifiable workflow.

4
00:00:21,738 --> 00:00:32,849
A creator enters a campaign prompt and receives an image plus a run ID, provider and model details, and a cryptographic verification receipt.

5
00:00:32,849 --> 00:00:34,781
Refinement preserves the relationship.

6
00:00:34,781 --> 00:00:44,442
The new result points back to its parent, so reviewers can move through the lineage instead of comparing disconnected downloads.

7
00:00:44,442 --> 00:00:51,205
Under the hood, Genblaze orchestrates the selected generative provider and produces a canonical manifest.

8
00:00:51,205 --> 00:00:55,070
The live submission uses NVIDIA NIM through Genblaze.

9
00:00:55,070 --> 00:01:03,765
Backblaze B2 stores the generated media and manifests using content-addressable keys, so identical bytes share one durable object.

10
00:01:03,765 --> 00:01:06,663
Verification does not trust database metadata.

11
00:01:06,663 --> 00:01:16,325
Provenance Studio fetches the stored B2 object, recomputes its SHA-256 digest, and compares that value with the signed workflow record.

12
00:01:16,325 --> 00:01:18,740
Here is the failure path.

13
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:24,537
In an isolated demonstration, changing one stored byte makes verification fail immediately.

14
00:01:24,537 --> 00:01:28,884
Restoring the original bytes makes the receipt pass again.

15
00:01:28,884 --> 00:01:33,715
The public production bucket is never altered for this demonstration.

16
00:01:33,715 --> 00:01:43,859
The browser experience includes parent-first lineage, media zoom and download, receipt refresh, a private judge-access token, and a strict generation limit.

17
00:01:43,859 --> 00:01:51,105
Live services stay disabled unless every required credential and the explicit enable flag are present.

18
00:01:51,105 --> 00:01:57,868
This draft reserves the final live segment for the authorized NVIDIA and Backblaze run.

19
00:01:57,868 --> 00:02:07,047
Once inserted, judges will see the generated asset, its B2-backed receipt, and the public deployment operating end to end.

20
00:02:07,047 --> 00:02:15,259
Provenance Studio gives creative teams speed without surrendering provenance: generate, refine, store, and verify every campaign asset.
